  "summary": "A kettle reboiler supplies the vapour that drives a distillation column. Liquid from the column bottom floods a horizontal tube bundle inside an enlarged shell; steam or hot oil inside the tubes boils part of the liquid. Vapour rises to the column through the top nozzles; the remaining liquid spills over a weir and leaves as bottom product.",
